      "worked_solution": "The denominators are $5$ and $10.$ We can make a common denominator of $10$ by splitting the shape on the left into $2$ parts vertically:  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/3d4839662bcac31bc197436b533da61e07ecf1ca301b3fa7613d433833e14028.png)\n\n \n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}6}{10} \\div \\dfrac{\\color{blue}7}{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}6} \\div {\\color{blue}7} = \\dfrac{6}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/96b55dc2d7a2c2051c899f3ba2770b06d47595459a58a9728d8f95d63c312dad.svg)\n\nHence, the missing number is $6.$",
